# Pagination

## Framework semantics

CakePHP paginates result sets via controller `$this->paginate()` (or PaginatorComponent patterns) over Table queries/finders. Pagination is HTTP list orchestration — not a place to dump complex domain query graphs without finders.

## Required behavior

- Build reusable query semantics in Table finders; paginate the finder from the controller.
- Preserve filter/sort query params consistently with project conventions (and Search when installed).
- Do not load unbounded result sets into memory when pagination is the product requirement.
- Keep page size limits sensible; reject client-controlled absurd limits unless explicitly allowed.

## Anti-patterns

- Copying huge `where`/`contain` stacks into every paginate call instead of a finder
- Unbounded `all()` for UI lists that should be paginated
- Do not invent Laravel LengthAwarePaginator APIs

## Review checklist

- [ ] List endpoints use CakePHP pagination (or documented alternative)
- [ ] Query reuse lives in finders/filters, not duplicated in controllers
- [ ] Contain/eager-load budgets stay reasonable per page
